Submitted Q & A                NannyMUD Times                        Page 16

  The Times is currently collecting questions for a monthly question
  article. We will collect questions from players at the newspaper stand
  and a chosen question will be published in every issue. Players can
  submit their answers to the current question at the stand, which will be
  published in the ensuing issue along with a new question.

  This months question is:

  * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
    Do you ever visit the NannyMUD website?
      -Bayar
  * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *


  Last months question was:

  * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
    Do you think it is worth the effort to change
    Nanny so that it would be more newbie oriented?
  * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *

  Auric:
    The newbie's purpose in (game) life is to transcend from being a 
    newbie to not being one.  The only "newbie orientation"  is to give 
    newbies enough help, encouragement and curiosity to move beyond the 
    stage of being one.  NannyMUD already meets the needs of newbies 
    superlatively.  To the same extent, I think it caters to the interests 
    of highly experienced (or ambitious) players poorly.  So my answer is 
    no.  I think attention needs to be bestowed on making this game more 
    exciting for dedicated, advanced players.  Newbies are already looked 
    after very well and needn't be worried about.

  Bayar:
    In my opinion, Nanny cannot be more newbie orianted than this.

  Astrodeath:
    I think there are a few changes that could help newbies at the
    start. There could be a question posed at the time of character
    creation: Are you new to NannyMUD? <yes/no> If the player answers
    yes, they get the Newbie Booklet, some generic equipment, a
    backpack containing a torch and rope, and is joined to the 
    Adventurers Guild. It might also be fun to add an all-game message 
    that announces the arrival of the newbie into the game.
    If the player answers no, they are just dropped into game, free to 
    pursue their plan.
    

